[thin] These locations retain the exact accepted Industrial foot's cavity boundaries, registration sockets, local edge intersections and three-millimetre exterior shell. The smallest readings lie at the source shoulder at CAD Z14; this coupon adds no fins or intermediate discs. Preserving those surfaces is necessary for this replication plate to compare cooling on the geometry with the reported supported-edge lifting. This entry accepts the geometry for an experiment; it does not qualify sub-millimetre material for production strength.
alternatives: Thickening or blending these locations would change contact geometry, local heat capacity and the lifting replication. A simplified solid foot would omit the original cavity and support pattern. Those are separate geometry candidates after this controlled comparison.
